{"duration_api_ms":211172,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"5da87cff-c5e4-4362-b606-35fd17ec6fc6","total_cost_usd":0.6173845,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":69920,"cache_read_input_tokens":307895,"output_tokens":30595,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":15945},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":69920,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":17804,"cache_read_input_tokens":87171,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1071},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":7570,"outputTokens":360,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0009370000000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":329,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":30595,"cacheReadInputTokens":307895,"cacheCreationInputTokens":69920,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6164475,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":15945,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":69920,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":14,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer\":\"numerical_auditor\",\"paper_id\":\"bicycle-infrastructure-paper\",\"run_status\":\"partial\",\"summary\":\"Most counts and shares in the paper reconcile. This covers the 70/36/34 pilot funnel, the 5+8+21 manual coding split, Tables 3 and 4 (33/34 = 97%), Table 6 (19+10+9+5 = 43; 19+10 = 29), the 18+26 = 44 ceremony split, Table 8 (266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579; every share recomputes), and the Figure 2 and Figure 4 values quoted in the text. I found five numerical problems. (1) The \\\"2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent)\\\" statement uses distinct openings as the numerator over an article denominator, while the paper itself counts 5 relevant articles. (2) Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article not relevant, but Table 3 shows the second coder coded it relevant. (3) The 96-article and 44-project totals cannot be verified, because the paper does not say whether the pilot and rounds 2–4 overlap. (4) Figure 1's \\\"2 distinct openings that took place\\\" conflicts with Table 2 footnote c, which says Grettefoss opened on 3 November. (5) The text says only Q1 2024 is missing from Figure 3, but the data gap is January–April 2024. The run is partial because I did not complete an entry-by-entry pass through numbers_in_text.json.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"NUM-001\",\"category\":\"numerator_unit_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"The sentence \\\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place\\\" uses the number of distinct openings (2) as the numerator over a denominator of articles. The paper's own Figure 1 and Section 3.1.4 count 5 relevant articles about those two openings (4 Homborsund, 1 Stod), which is 14.7% of 34, or 3 of 34 (8.8%) after the two pre-opening Homborsund articles are excluded. The Figure 1 caption makes the same unit switch with \\\"2 of 70 search hits\\\".\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 Pilot sample\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"2/34 = 5.9%, so the arithmetic matches the reported 6 percent. The numerator, however, is the count of distinct openings (Figure 1: \\\"Distinct openings that took place 2\\\"), not articles. Section 3.1.4 says \\\"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found. Four of the articles mention Homborsund and one Stod.\\\" Figure 1 reports 5 articles coded relevant (15% retained). The article-level share concerning an opening is therefore 5/34 = 14.7%, or 3/34 = 8.8% after the pre-opening articles are excluded (Section 4). The same units issue applies to \\\"Only 2 of 70 search hits\\\" in the Figure 1 caption, because several of the 70 hits are duplicates of those articles. The yield is stated at the project level but written as an article-level share.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Sentence and Figure 1 chart labels (5 coded relevant, 15% retained; 2 distinct openings) also checked on the page 4 image.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found. Four of the articles mention Homborsund and one Stod.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Gives the 5 relevant articles behind the 2 openings.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"2 of 34 unique articles concern an opening that took place\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"The count of 2 is of projects. The paper's own article-level count is 5 (or 3 after exclusions).\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"arithmetic\",\"operation\":\"ratio\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"5\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Articles coded relevant that report the two openings\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"34\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"n/a\",\"context\":\"Unique articles in the pilot\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"reported\":{\"value\":\"6\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Share of unique articles said to concern an opening that took place\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0.5\",\"scale\":\"percent\"},\"computed_value\":\"14.7 (percent; 5/34 = 0.147)\",\"tolerance\":\"0.5 percentage points\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"The 6 percent equals 2 openings / 34 articles. The article-level share implied by the paper's 5 relevant articles is 14.7 percent, which is the 15 percent shown in Figure 1. After excluding the two pre-opening Homborsund articles it is 3/34 = 8.8 percent.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The authors may intend a project-level yield but wrote an article-level denominator.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"State the unit explicitly. Either report 2 distinct openings among 34 articles, or report the article-based share with the stated inclusion rule.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Rewrite the sentence, and the Figure 1 caption's \\\"2 of 70 search hits\\\", so that numerator and denominator use the same unit (articles, or projects).\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-002\",\"category\":\"cross_source_count_conflict\",\"finding_summary\":\"Footnote 3 says the Stord project was coded not relevant by both human coders. Table 3 and the Section 4.1 text show that the second coder coded the Stord article relevant, since this is the single human-coder disagreement.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)\",\"text_quote\":\"coded as not relevant by both human coders\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"The 44 projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4).\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Table 3 (pilot coder rows, second coder columns) has Not relevant / Relevant = 1. That is the one article the coders disagree on. Section 4.1 identifies it as the Stord municipality/Vestland dispute article: \\\"The only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County over a pedestrian crossing.\\\" The pilot coder coded it not relevant, so the second coder must have coded it relevant (second-coder relevant total 4 = 3 + 1). If both coders had coded it not relevant, that cell would be 0 and agreement would be 34/34. Section 4.2 says the LLM majority also coded it relevant. Footnote 3 therefore conflicts with Table 3.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"Footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"coded as not relevant by both human coders\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Footnote text; the quote wraps across lines in the extraction.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4.1 / Table 3\",\"text_quote\":\"Not relevant 1 30 31\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 3 body row. The parser-quality notes say the Table 3 body cells match the image; header alignment was taken from the layout (pilot coder rows, second coder columns).\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Stord project coded not relevant by both human coders\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"Table 3 has one pilot-not-relevant / second-coder-relevant article, identified in the text as the Stord article.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"1\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Table 3 cell: pilot coder Not relevant, second coder Relevant\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"0\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"Stord project/article\",\"denominator\":\"n/a\",\"context\":\"Number of human coders who coded the Stord article relevant, as implied by footnote 3 (both coded not relevant), which gives zero off-diagonal cases\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Both refer to the same pilot articles and the same relevance coding by the pilot and second coder. The Section 4.1 text ties the disagreement cell to the Stord article.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"Table 3 implies one article coded relevant by the second coder only, namely the Stord article. Footnote 3 implies zero.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The footnote may refer to the pilot coder and the LLM-agnostic 'validation' coding, or may be an editing error. The paper does not say.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"Reconcile footnote 3 with Table 3 and say which coder(s) coded the Stord article relevant.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Correct footnote 3 (or Table 3) so that the Stord article's coding by each human coder is consistent, and restate the 44-project count basis accordingly.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-003\",\"category\":\"unverifiable_total\",\"finding_summary\":\"The totals of 96 article records and 44 projects (92 + 4 and 43 + 1) cannot be verified as non-overlapping. Rounds 2–4 cover October 2025–October 2026 and the pilot covers 2 September–10 October 2026, and the paper does not say whether pilot articles are excluded from rounds 2–4.\",\"issue_type\":\"cannot_verify\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)\",\"text_quote\":\"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"In total, 96 article records across the pilot and the later rounds reported an opening, resulting in 44 unique projects.\",\"assessment\":\"cannot_verify\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":\"The paper does not state whether the pilot articles (2 Sep–10 Oct 2026) are excluded from rounds 2–4 (published Oct 2025–Oct 2026), so it is not possible to tell whether the 4 pilot articles add to the 92 or duplicate them. Footnote 3 also says the 44 projects are the 43 plus Stord, which appears only in the pilot, which implies the pilot's Homborsund and Stod projects are already among the 43.\",\"evidence_summary\":\"The additions 92 + 4 = 96 and 43 + 1 = 44 are arithmetically consistent. Section 5 gives the 3,187 articles of rounds 2–4 as published between October 2025 and October 2026, and Section 3.1.2 gives the pilot window as 2 September–10 October 2026. The windows overlap. If the pilot's Homborsund and Stod articles are among the 43 projects, the same articles may enter the 92 and the 4. The four pilot articles match the LLM-relevant total in Table 4 (3 + Stord), but that does not show they are separate from the 92. Table 7 and the Section 6.3 ratios (18 + 26 = 44; 17 + 2 = 19 day-dated) rest on the 44.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 / footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Footnote text.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 9 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_009.md\",\"page\":9,\"page_label\":\"9\",\"section\":\"5 Results\",\"text_quote\":\"published between October 2025 and October 2026\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-521bfe93a764059cd1136195\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Round 2–4 publication window.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"96 articles = 92 + 4 pilot articles; 44 projects = 43 + 1\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"cannot_verify\",\"note\":\"Overlap between pilot and rounds 2–4 is not stated.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"Are the 4 pilot articles and the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 disjoint, so that 96 and 44 are correct totals?\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"92\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"Rounds 2–4, published Oct 2025–Oct 2026\",\"denominator\":\"3,187 articles coded\",\"context\":\"Articles reporting an opening in Section 5\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"4\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"Pilot run, 2 Sep–10 Oct 2026\",\"denominator\":\"34 pilot articles\",\"context\":\"Pilot articles counted in the 96\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"missing_information\":[\"Whether pilot articles are excluded from rounds 2–4\",\"Which project each of the four pilot articles belongs to, and whether those projects are among the 43\",\"Round definitions (what rounds 1–4 are)\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"State whether the pilot and rounds 2–4 overlap, and give a deduplicated article and project count for the combined sample.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-004\",\"category\":\"count_timing_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"Figure 1 reports 2 distinct openings that took place, but Table 2 footnote c states that the Grettefoss Bridge opening was confirmed on 3 November 2026, before the 9 November manuscript date. That gives 3 pilot projects that opened, while Figure 1 and the surrounding text still treat Grettefoss as a planned/unclear case.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4 / Table 2\",\"text_quote\":\"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.\",\"precision\":\"partial\"},\"claim_text\":\"Distinct openings that took place: 2 (Figure 1); \\\"Only 2 of 70 search hits concern a cycling infrastructure opening that actually took place\\\".\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Figure 1 counts 2 distinct openings that took place (Homborsund and Stod/Steinkjer). Table 2 footnote c says Grettefoss Bridge is \\\"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned\\\", even though its status column still says Planned. The paper does not state the reference date for 'took place'. If it is the end of the pilot window (10 October) the count of 2 holds. If it is the manuscript date, the count would be 3 (Tromsø is delayed to 27 November).\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"Table 2 footnote c\",\"text_quote\":\"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Footnote marker 'c' is attached to the word in the extraction, so the quote omits it. Table 2 row shows 'Grettefoss Bridge Flesberg 1 3 Nov 2026c Planned'.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"Figure 1\",\"text_quote\":\"Distinct openings that took place\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Chart label; value 2 confirmed on the page 4 image.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Only 2 distinct openings took place\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"Count depends on an unstated reference date.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"2\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"distinct openings\",\"sample\":\"Pilot, 70 hits / 34 unique articles\",\"denominator\":\"n/a\",\"context\":\"Figure 1 count of distinct openings that took place\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"3\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"distinct openings\",\"sample\":\"Pilot projects in Table 2 with status Opened as of the manuscript date (Homborsund, Stod, and Grettefoss per footnote c)\",\"denominator\":\"n/a\",\"context\":\"Number of Table 2 projects that opened, counting footnote c as of 9 November 2026\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Comparable only if both counts use the same reference date. Figure 1 does not state its date, and Table 2 footnotes use 6 November.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"2 openings in Figure 1 against 3 projects that have opened according to Table 2's own footnote.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"Figure 1 may count only openings that had occurred by the pilot cut-off (10 October 2026).\",\"suggested_correction\":\"State the reference date for 'opening that took place' in Figure 1 and Table 2, and update the Table 2 status for Grettefoss if the later date is used.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"State the cut-off date for the count in Figure 1, or update the count and the Table 2 status column to the same date.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-005\",\"category\":\"time_period_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"The text says \\\"The first quarter of 2024 is missing\\\" from the quarterly Figure 3, but the Appendix A.1 and Figure 3 caption describe the data gap as January to April 2024, which also removes April from Q2 2024. Figure 3 plots a Q2 2024 point, so the quarterly share for that quarter is based on a partial quarter, which the paper does not say.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 3\",\"text_quote\":\"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Appendix A.1: \\\"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing\\\". Figure 3 caption: \\\"The gap in 2024 is due to missing listing text from January to April 2024.\\\" That is four months, across Q1 and one month of Q2. On the page 16 image, a point appears after the gap at roughly the start of Q2 2024, so that quarterly value would rest on May–June only. The effect on the series is probably small but is not disclosed.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 16 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2\",\"text_quote\":\"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Passage wraps across lines in the extraction. Plotted points inspected on the page 16 image.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 15 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_015.md\",\"page\":15,\"page_label\":\"15\",\"section\":\"A.1\",\"text_quote\":\"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Gap definition.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Only Q1 2024 is missing\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"The gap is four months, and April belongs to Q2.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"1\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"quarters\",\"sample\":\"Quarterly series, 2020–2026\",\"denominator\":\"n/a\",\"context\":\"Number of quarters said to be missing in 2024 (first quarter)\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"4\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"months\",\"sample\":\"Listing text data, January 2020–October 2026\",\"denominator\":\"n/a\",\"context\":\"Months of missing listing text in 2024 (January to April)\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Both describe the same listing-text gap. A quarter is three months, so four missing months cannot fit within one quarter.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"One missing quarter (3 months) in the text against a 4-month gap in the appendix and caption.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The text may be shorthand, with the partial Q2 2024 quarter plotted from May–June listings.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"Say that Q1 2024 is missing and Q2 2024 covers only May–June, or drop the Q2 2024 point.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Align the text with the January–April gap and state how the Q2 2024 observation was computed.\"}],\"notes\":[\"Arithmetic identities checked with no issue: 70-36=34; 34/70=48.6% (49%); 5/34=14.7% (15%); 5+8+21=34; 21+8+2=31 (Tables 3 and 4 'not relevant' row); (3+30)/34=97.06%; 1/34=2.9% (3%); 19+10+9+5=43; 19+10=29; 17+2=19; 18+26=44; 92+4=96; 43+1=44; 266,625+433,954=700,579; every Table 8 share recomputes to the stated 0.1 pp; Table 8 type rows sum to 346,827 > 266,625, as the note says (overlapping types); county shares in the text match Figure 4; Figure 2 sykkel 9.8% equals Table 8 'The word bicycle' 9.8%.\",\"Table 5 'Length 2,132 m' versus road-reference ranges 0–1492 plus 0–641 (= 2,133 m) differs by 1 m; this is rounding-compatible and not reported. 'One month before the opening' matches 4 Sep to 5 Oct 2026.\",\"Section 6.2's wording 'between a third and a half' versus Table 7 (34%–55% of 44 projects, except 'Reasons for delay' at 4/44 = 9%) is approximate and not reported as a defect.\",\"Parser-quality guidance was respected: table CSV/markdown was not used for cell values. Values came from the page text, with Figures 1 and 3 read from the page images (pages 4 and 16). The table PNG crops were not individually viewed in this pass.\",\"External figures (Copenhagen +60%, Fyhri up to 5 pp, Bartik 96%) are outside the retained evidence and were not checked.\",\"I did not complete an entry-by-entry pass through numbers_in_text.json; the numeric statements were covered by reading full_text.md in full instead. This is listed under missing_checks.\"],\"completion\":{\"version\":1,\"state\":\"partial\",\"scope_description\":\"Numerical audit of the bicycle-infrastructure-paper parsed artifacts: a full read of full_text.md, recomputation of counts, shares and identities in the text, Tables 1–9 (via page text, given the parser-quality warnings) and Figures 1–4, and visual inspection of the page 4 and page 16 images.\",\"checks_completed\":[\"Read the parser-quality guidance and used page text and images instead of the unreliable table CSV/markdown\",\"Recomputed the pilot funnel, manual-coding split, Table 3/4 agreement rates, internal-consistency rate, Table 6 totals and date-precision sums, ceremony split, Table 8 identities and shares\",\"Compared text percentages with Figure 2 and Figure 4 values and Figure 3's plotted range\",\"Checked consistency of 92/43/96/44 counts across Sections 5, 6 and footnote 3, and of Table 2 footnotes against Figure 1\",\"Checked for percent vs percentage-point and article-vs-project unit conflation\"],\"missing_checks\":[\"Systematic entry-by-entry pass through numbers_in_text.json (not performed; full_text.md was read in full instead)\"],\"evidence_limitations\":[\"Structured table cells are unreliable per the parser-quality guidance; table values were taken from page text. Table PNG crops were not individually viewed.\",\"Only page images 4 and 16 were viewed.\",\"External literature figures were not verified.\",\"Round definitions (rounds 1–4) are not given, so overlap between rounds cannot be established.\"]},\"coverage\":[{\"item_id\":\"assigned_remit\",\"source_object_ids\":[],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read full_text.md in full, recomputed numeric statements and identities, and cross-checked text against tables and figures. The entry-by-entry pass through numbers_in_text.json was not performed.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Five findings (NUM-001 to NUM-005). The numbers_in_text.json pass is missing, so the run is partial.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-001\",\"NUM-002\",\"NUM-003\",\"NUM-004\",\"NUM-005\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"sampled\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read the Figure 1 chart values from the page 4 image and text (70, 34 at 49%, 5 at 15%, 2) and recomputed the retention percentages and the 2/34 statement.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"The percentages recompute (34/70 = 48.6%, 5/34 = 14.7%). The '2 of 70' and '2 of 34' statements use projects as the numerator (NUM-001), and the '2 distinct openings' count conflicts with Table 2 footnote c (NUM-004).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-001\",\"NUM-004\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Compared Figure 2 bar values on the page 16 image with the text ('around 5 percent', 9.8%) and Table 8, and checked the sort order and 20-word count.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Values and ordering agree with the text and with Table 8's 'The word bicycle' 9.8%. Per-category word shares are consistent with the Table 8 type shares (a union cannot exceed the sum of its member words).\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read the Figure 3 plotted series on the page 16 image: start about 35%, end about 44%, dip in late 2023, gap in 2024. Compared with the text and the Appendix A.1 gap definition.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"The 35%-to-44% rise (about 9 pp) and the late-2023 dip agree with the text. The gap description is inconsistent (Q1 versus January–April) (NUM-005).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-005\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Compared Figure 4 county shares (from page 17 text) with the text: Oslo 61, Akershus 52, Telemark 14, Nordland 13, Møre og Romsdal 7; counted 15 counties.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All quoted county shares round correctly from the plotted labels. The national 38 percent is consistent with Table 8. Lowest three counties are as stated.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 1 from page 5 text. It holds no summary statistics; I checked its numbers (3 km, 3.5 m, 4 articles in 2 newspapers) against Table 7 and the Homborsund coverage count in Table 2.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"The only counts in Table 1 (Homborsund covered by 4 articles) agree with Table 2 and Section 3.1.4.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-dbc6f4a9a830bbbd128e371e\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-dbc6f4a9a830bbbd128e371e\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 2 rows and footnotes from page 5 text (the structured markdown is truncated). Checked article counts (4+1+1+1), dates and weekday resolution (5 Oct 2026 is a Monday).\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Counts and dates are internally consistent. Footnote c (Grettefoss opened 3 November) conflicts with Figure 1's count of 2 openings (NUM-004).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-004\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-e3774f186493fe1cf3afe556\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-e3774f186493fe1cf3afe556\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Recomputed the Table 3 margins (3+0, 1+30, 3+1, 0+30, total 34) and agreement (33/34 = 97.06%); compared the off-diagonal case with footnote 3 on page 10.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Margins and the 97% figure are correct. The off-diagonal Stord case conflicts with footnote 3 (NUM-002).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-002\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-a9068469a80185aaa27470fa\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-a9068469a80185aaa27470fa\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Recomputed the Table 4 margins and agreement (33/34 = 97.06%); compared with the text on the 3/3 date agreement and the one-in-three-runs disagreement.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"The arithmetic is correct. Identical cell counts to Table 3 are consistent with the text, which names the same Stord article as the disagreement.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-e6d7a21f6dac33af8ecba464\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-e6d7a21f6dac33af8ecba464\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 5 from page 9 text. Checked the length (2,132 m) against the road-reference ranges (1492 + 641 = 2,133 m), 4 Sep to 5 Oct as 'one month', and the date and weekday.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"A 1 m difference in length is rounding-compatible. The one-month gap and the Monday weekday are consistent. Gradient, climb and bridge values have no cross-check available in the paper.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-ff90f28affccf4abf5c4e78c\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-ff90f28affccf4abf5c4e78c\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 6 from page 10 text (the markdown interleaves panels). Summed date-precision counts (19+10+9+5 = 43) and 19+10 = 29, and compared 92, 43, 50 outlets and 14 of 15 counties with Section 5 and the Figure 4 county list.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"The sums match the abstract, introduction and conclusion. 14 of 15 counties matches 'all counties except Østfold'.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-2c51ead4a14e19e7c3de50a9\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-2c51ead4a14e19e7c3de50a9\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 7 counts from page 11 text. Computed the shares of 44 (15/44 to 24/44, 42/44, 4/44) and compared with the 'between a third and a half' wording. Checked the Section 6.3 split 18+26 = 44 and 17+2 = 19.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"The shares are broadly consistent with the wording. The 44-project base depends on the unverifiable 96/44 totals (NUM-003).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-003\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-8cd1361a5f77a70c5008ee4d\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-8cd1361a5f77a70c5008ee4d\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Used the page 15 text (the markdown splits thousands). Verified 266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579, all shares to 0.1 pp, and that the type rows sum to 346,827, which exceeds the any-mention count as the note states.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All identities and shares hold. The abstract 38 percent and the 452,118 mentions across 266,625 listings agree with the table.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-b0c2f2010110ab92e8c28a1c\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-b0c2f2010110ab92e8c28a1c\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 9 (word-part classification) for numeric content.\",\"status\":\"not_applicable\",\"reason\":\"No quantitative values. It is a keyword classification table. Its classification rules were not tested against the Table 8 counts, since the underlying listing data are not available.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer":"numerical_auditor","paper_id":"bicycle-infrastructure-paper","run_status":"partial","summary":"Most counts and shares in the paper reconcile. This covers the 70/36/34 pilot funnel, the 5+8+21 manual coding split, Tables 3 and 4 (33/34 = 97%), Table 6 (19+10+9+5 = 43; 19+10 = 29), the 18+26 = 44 ceremony split, Table 8 (266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579; every share recomputes), and the Figure 2 and Figure 4 values quoted in the text. I found five numerical problems. (1) The \"2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent)\" statement uses distinct openings as the numerator over an article denominator, while the paper itself counts 5 relevant articles. (2) Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article not relevant, but Table 3 shows the second coder coded it relevant. (3) The 96-article and 44-project totals cannot be verified, because the paper does not say whether the pilot and rounds 2–4 overlap. (4) Figure 1's \"2 distinct openings that took place\" conflicts with Table 2 footnote c, which says Grettefoss opened on 3 November. (5) The text says only Q1 2024 is missing from Figure 3, but the data gap is January–April 2024. The run is partial because I did not complete an entry-by-entry pass through numbers_in_text.json.","findings":[{"id":"NUM-001","category":"numerator_unit_mismatch","finding_summary":"The sentence \"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place\" uses the number of distinct openings (2) as the numerator over a denominator of articles. The paper's own Figure 1 and Section 3.1.4 count 5 relevant articles about those two openings (4 Homborsund, 1 Stod), which is 14.7% of 34, or 3 of 34 (8.8%) after the two pre-opening Homborsund articles are excluded. The Figure 1 caption makes the same unit switch with \"2 of 70 search hits\".","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","location":{"page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2 Pilot sample","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"2/34 = 5.9%, so the arithmetic matches the reported 6 percent. The numerator, however, is the count of distinct openings (Figure 1: \"Distinct openings that took place 2\"), not articles. Section 3.1.4 says \"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found. Four of the articles mention Homborsund and one Stod.\" Figure 1 reports 5 articles coded relevant (15% retained). The article-level share concerning an opening is therefore 5/34 = 14.7%, or 3/34 = 8.8% after the pre-opening articles are excluded (Section 4). The same units issue applies to \"Only 2 of 70 search hits\" in the Figure 1 caption, because several of the 70 hits are duplicates of those articles. The yield is stated at the project level but written as an article-level share.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 4 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Sentence and Figure 1 chart labels (5 coded relevant, 15% retained; 2 distinct openings) also checked on the page 4 image."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 5 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4","text_quote":"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found. Four of the articles mention Homborsund and one Stod.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Gives the 5 relevant articles behind the 2 openings."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"2 of 34 unique articles concern an opening that took place","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"The count of 2 is of projects. The paper's own article-level count is 5 (or 3 after exclusions)."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"arithmetic","operation":"ratio","quantities":[{"value":"5","source_id":"S2","unit":"articles","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Articles coded relevant that report the two openings","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"34","source_id":"S1","unit":"articles","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"n/a","context":"Unique articles in the pilot","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"reported":{"value":"6","source_id":"S1","unit":"percent","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Share of unique articles said to concern an opening that took place","rounding_half_width":"0.5","scale":"percent"},"computed_value":"14.7 (percent; 5/34 = 0.147)","tolerance":"0.5 percentage points","observed_discrepancy":"The 6 percent equals 2 openings / 34 articles. The article-level share implied by the paper's 5 relevant articles is 14.7 percent, which is the 15 percent shown in Figure 1. After excluding the two pre-opening Homborsund articles it is 3/34 = 8.8 percent.","possible_explanation":"The authors may intend a project-level yield but wrote an article-level denominator.","suggested_correction":"State the unit explicitly. Either report 2 distinct openings among 34 articles, or report the article-based share with the stated inclusion rule."},"suggested_fix":"Rewrite the sentence, and the Figure 1 caption's \"2 of 70 search hits\", so that numerator and denominator use the same unit (articles, or projects)."},{"id":"NUM-002","category":"cross_source_count_conflict","finding_summary":"Footnote 3 says the Stord project was coded not relevant by both human coders. Table 3 and the Section 4.1 text show that the second coder coded the Stord article relevant, since this is the single human-coder disagreement.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)","text_quote":"coded as not relevant by both human coders","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"The 44 projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4).","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Table 3 (pilot coder rows, second coder columns) has Not relevant / Relevant = 1. That is the one article the coders disagree on. Section 4.1 identifies it as the Stord municipality/Vestland dispute article: \"The only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County over a pedestrian crossing.\" The pilot coder coded it not relevant, so the second coder must have coded it relevant (second-coder relevant total 4 = 3 + 1). If both coders had coded it not relevant, that cell would be 0 and agreement would be 34/34. Section 4.2 says the LLM majority also coded it relevant. Footnote 3 therefore conflicts with Table 3.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"Footnote 3","text_quote":"coded as not relevant by both human coders","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Footnote text; the quote wraps across lines in the extraction."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 7 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4.1 / Table 3","text_quote":"Not relevant 1 30 31","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 3 body row. The parser-quality notes say the Table 3 body cells match the image; header alignment was taken from the layout (pilot coder rows, second coder columns)."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Stord project coded not relevant by both human coders","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"Table 3 has one pilot-not-relevant / second-coder-relevant article, identified in the text as the Stord article."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"1","source_id":"S2","unit":"articles","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Table 3 cell: pilot coder Not relevant, second coder Relevant","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"0","source_id":"S1","unit":"articles","sample":"Stord project/article","denominator":"n/a","context":"Number of human coders who coded the Stord article relevant, as implied by footnote 3 (both coded not relevant), which gives zero off-diagonal cases","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Both refer to the same pilot articles and the same relevance coding by the pilot and second coder. The Section 4.1 text ties the disagreement cell to the Stord article.","observed_discrepancy":"Table 3 implies one article coded relevant by the second coder only, namely the Stord article. Footnote 3 implies zero.","possible_explanation":"The footnote may refer to the pilot coder and the LLM-agnostic 'validation' coding, or may be an editing error. The paper does not say.","suggested_correction":"Reconcile footnote 3 with Table 3 and say which coder(s) coded the Stord article relevant."},"suggested_fix":"Correct footnote 3 (or Table 3) so that the Stord article's coding by each human coder is consistent, and restate the 44-project count basis accordingly."},{"id":"NUM-003","category":"unverifiable_total","finding_summary":"The totals of 96 article records and 44 projects (92 + 4 and 43 + 1) cannot be verified as non-overlapping. Rounds 2–4 cover October 2025–October 2026 and the pilot covers 2 September–10 October 2026, and the paper does not say whether pilot articles are excluded from rounds 2–4.","issue_type":"cannot_verify","severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)","text_quote":"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"In total, 96 article records across the pilot and the later rounds reported an opening, resulting in 44 unique projects.","assessment":"cannot_verify","cannot_verify_reason":"The paper does not state whether the pilot articles (2 Sep–10 Oct 2026) are excluded from rounds 2–4 (published Oct 2025–Oct 2026), so it is not possible to tell whether the 4 pilot articles add to the 92 or duplicate them. Footnote 3 also says the 44 projects are the 43 plus Stord, which appears only in the pilot, which implies the pilot's Homborsund and Stod projects are already among the 43.","evidence_summary":"The additions 92 + 4 = 96 and 43 + 1 = 44 are arithmetically consistent. Section 5 gives the 3,187 articles of rounds 2–4 as published between October 2025 and October 2026, and Section 3.1.2 gives the pilot window as 2 September–10 October 2026. The windows overlap. If the pilot's Homborsund and Stod articles are among the 43 projects, the same articles may enter the 92 and the 4. The four pilot articles match the LLM-relevant total in Table 4 (3 + Stord), but that does not show they are separate from the 92. Table 7 and the Section 6.3 ratios (18 + 26 = 44; 17 + 2 = 19 day-dated) rest on the 44.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 / footnote 3","text_quote":"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Footnote text."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 9 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_009.md","page":9,"page_label":"9","section":"5 Results","text_quote":"published between October 2025 and October 2026","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-521bfe93a764059cd1136195","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Round 2–4 publication window."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"96 articles = 92 + 4 pilot articles; 44 projects = 43 + 1","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"cannot_verify","note":"Overlap between pilot and rounds 2–4 is not stated."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"underdetermined","question":"Are the 4 pilot articles and the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 disjoint, so that 96 and 44 are correct totals?","quantities":[{"value":"92","source_id":"S1","unit":"articles","sample":"Rounds 2–4, published Oct 2025–Oct 2026","denominator":"3,187 articles coded","context":"Articles reporting an opening in Section 5","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"4","source_id":"S1","unit":"articles","sample":"Pilot run, 2 Sep–10 Oct 2026","denominator":"34 pilot articles","context":"Pilot articles counted in the 96","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"missing_information":["Whether pilot articles are excluded from rounds 2–4","Which project each of the four pilot articles belongs to, and whether those projects are among the 43","Round definitions (what rounds 1–4 are)"],"status":"unresolved"},"suggested_fix":"State whether the pilot and rounds 2–4 overlap, and give a deduplicated article and project count for the combined sample."},{"id":"NUM-004","category":"count_timing_inconsistency","finding_summary":"Figure 1 reports 2 distinct openings that took place, but Table 2 footnote c states that the Grettefoss Bridge opening was confirmed on 3 November 2026, before the 9 November manuscript date. That gives 3 pilot projects that opened, while Figure 1 and the surrounding text still treat Grettefoss as a planned/unclear case.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4 / Table 2","text_quote":"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.","precision":"partial"},"claim_text":"Distinct openings that took place: 2 (Figure 1); \"Only 2 of 70 search hits concern a cycling infrastructure opening that actually took place\".","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Figure 1 counts 2 distinct openings that took place (Homborsund and Stod/Steinkjer). Table 2 footnote c says Grettefoss Bridge is \"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned\", even though its status column still says Planned. The paper does not state the reference date for 'took place'. If it is the end of the pilot window (10 October) the count of 2 holds. If it is the manuscript date, the count would be 3 (Tromsø is delayed to 27 November).","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 5 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"Table 2 footnote c","text_quote":"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Footnote marker 'c' is attached to the word in the extraction, so the quote omits it. Table 2 row shows 'Grettefoss Bridge Flesberg 1 3 Nov 2026c Planned'."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 4 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"Figure 1","text_quote":"Distinct openings that took place","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Chart label; value 2 confirmed on the page 4 image."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Only 2 distinct openings took place","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"Count depends on an unstated reference date."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"2","source_id":"S2","unit":"distinct openings","sample":"Pilot, 70 hits / 34 unique articles","denominator":"n/a","context":"Figure 1 count of distinct openings that took place","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"3","source_id":"S1","unit":"distinct openings","sample":"Pilot projects in Table 2 with status Opened as of the manuscript date (Homborsund, Stod, and Grettefoss per footnote c)","denominator":"n/a","context":"Number of Table 2 projects that opened, counting footnote c as of 9 November 2026","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Comparable only if both counts use the same reference date. Figure 1 does not state its date, and Table 2 footnotes use 6 November.","observed_discrepancy":"2 openings in Figure 1 against 3 projects that have opened according to Table 2's own footnote.","possible_explanation":"Figure 1 may count only openings that had occurred by the pilot cut-off (10 October 2026).","suggested_correction":"State the reference date for 'opening that took place' in Figure 1 and Table 2, and update the Table 2 status for Grettefoss if the later date is used."},"suggested_fix":"State the cut-off date for the count in Figure 1, or update the count and the Table 2 status column to the same date."},{"id":"NUM-005","category":"time_period_mismatch","finding_summary":"The text says \"The first quarter of 2024 is missing\" from the quarterly Figure 3, but the Appendix A.1 and Figure 3 caption describe the data gap as January to April 2024, which also removes April from Q2 2024. Figure 3 plots a Q2 2024 point, so the quarterly share for that quarter is based on a partial quarter, which the paper does not say.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 / Figure 3","text_quote":"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Appendix A.1: \"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing\". Figure 3 caption: \"The gap in 2024 is due to missing listing text from January to April 2024.\" That is four months, across Q1 and one month of Q2. On the page 16 image, a point appears after the gap at roughly the start of Q2 2024, so that quarterly value would rest on May–June only. The effect on the series is probably small but is not disclosed.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 16 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2","text_quote":"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Passage wraps across lines in the extraction. Plotted points inspected on the page 16 image."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 15 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_015.md","page":15,"page_label":"15","section":"A.1","text_quote":"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Gap definition."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Only Q1 2024 is missing","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"The gap is four months, and April belongs to Q2."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"1","source_id":"S1","unit":"quarters","sample":"Quarterly series, 2020–2026","denominator":"n/a","context":"Number of quarters said to be missing in 2024 (first quarter)","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"4","source_id":"S2","unit":"months","sample":"Listing text data, January 2020–October 2026","denominator":"n/a","context":"Months of missing listing text in 2024 (January to April)","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Both describe the same listing-text gap. A quarter is three months, so four missing months cannot fit within one quarter.","observed_discrepancy":"One missing quarter (3 months) in the text against a 4-month gap in the appendix and caption.","possible_explanation":"The text may be shorthand, with the partial Q2 2024 quarter plotted from May–June listings.","suggested_correction":"Say that Q1 2024 is missing and Q2 2024 covers only May–June, or drop the Q2 2024 point."},"suggested_fix":"Align the text with the January–April gap and state how the Q2 2024 observation was computed."}],"notes":["Arithmetic identities checked with no issue: 70-36=34; 34/70=48.6% (49%); 5/34=14.7% (15%); 5+8+21=34; 21+8+2=31 (Tables 3 and 4 'not relevant' row); (3+30)/34=97.06%; 1/34=2.9% (3%); 19+10+9+5=43; 19+10=29; 17+2=19; 18+26=44; 92+4=96; 43+1=44; 266,625+433,954=700,579; every Table 8 share recomputes to the stated 0.1 pp; Table 8 type rows sum to 346,827 > 266,625, as the note says (overlapping types); county shares in the text match Figure 4; Figure 2 sykkel 9.8% equals Table 8 'The word bicycle' 9.8%.","Table 5 'Length 2,132 m' versus road-reference ranges 0–1492 plus 0–641 (= 2,133 m) differs by 1 m; this is rounding-compatible and not reported. 'One month before the opening' matches 4 Sep to 5 Oct 2026.","Section 6.2's wording 'between a third and a half' versus Table 7 (34%–55% of 44 projects, except 'Reasons for delay' at 4/44 = 9%) is approximate and not reported as a defect.","Parser-quality guidance was respected: table CSV/markdown was not used for cell values. Values came from the page text, with Figures 1 and 3 read from the page images (pages 4 and 16). The table PNG crops were not individually viewed in this pass.","External figures (Copenhagen +60%, Fyhri up to 5 pp, Bartik 96%) are outside the retained evidence and were not checked.","I did not complete an entry-by-entry pass through numbers_in_text.json; the numeric statements were covered by reading full_text.md in full instead. This is listed under missing_checks."],"completion":{"version":1,"state":"partial","scope_description":"Numerical audit of the bicycle-infrastructure-paper parsed artifacts: a full read of full_text.md, recomputation of counts, shares and identities in the text, Tables 1–9 (via page text, given the parser-quality warnings) and Figures 1–4, and visual inspection of the page 4 and page 16 images.","checks_completed":["Read the parser-quality guidance and used page text and images instead of the unreliable table CSV/markdown","Recomputed the pilot funnel, manual-coding split, Table 3/4 agreement rates, internal-consistency rate, Table 6 totals and date-precision sums, ceremony split, Table 8 identities and shares","Compared text percentages with Figure 2 and Figure 4 values and Figure 3's plotted range","Checked consistency of 92/43/96/44 counts across Sections 5, 6 and footnote 3, and of Table 2 footnotes against Figure 1","Checked for percent vs percentage-point and article-vs-project unit conflation"],"missing_checks":["Systematic entry-by-entry pass through numbers_in_text.json (not performed; full_text.md was read in full instead)"],"evidence_limitations":["Structured table cells are unreliable per the parser-quality guidance; table values were taken from page text. Table PNG crops were not individually viewed.","Only page images 4 and 16 were viewed.","External literature figures were not verified.","Round definitions (rounds 1–4) are not given, so overlap between rounds cannot be established."]},"coverage":[{"item_id":"assigned_remit","source_object_ids":[],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Read full_text.md in full, recomputed numeric statements and identities, and cross-checked text against tables and figures. The entry-by-entry pass through numbers_in_text.json was not performed.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"Five findings (NUM-001 to NUM-005). The numbers_in_text.json pass is missing, so the run is partial.","finding_ids":["NUM-001","NUM-002","NUM-003","NUM-004","NUM-005"],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"sampled"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce","source_object_ids":["OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Read the Figure 1 chart values from the page 4 image and text (70, 34 at 49%, 5 at 15%, 2) and recomputed the retention percentages and the 2/34 statement.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"The percentages recompute (34/70 = 48.6%, 5/34 = 14.7%). The '2 of 70' and '2 of 34' statements use projects as the numerator (NUM-001), and the '2 distinct openings' count conflicts with Table 2 footnote c (NUM-004).","finding_ids":["NUM-001","NUM-004"],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa","source_object_ids":["OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Compared Figure 2 bar values on the page 16 image with the text ('around 5 percent', 9.8%) and Table 8, and checked the sort order and 20-word count.","status":"checked_no_issue","reason":"Values and ordering agree with the text and with Table 8's 'The word bicycle' 9.8%. Per-category word shares are consistent with the Table 8 type shares (a union cannot exceed the sum of its member words).","finding_ids":[],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798","source_object_ids":["OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Read the Figure 3 plotted series on the page 16 image: start about 35%, end about 44%, dip in late 2023, gap in 2024. Compared with the text and the Appendix A.1 gap definition.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"The 35%-to-44% rise (about 9 pp) and the late-2023 dip agree with the text. The gap description is inconsistent (Q1 versus January–April) (NUM-005).","finding_ids":["NUM-005"],"attempted":true,"importance":"peripheral","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item